entry.summary:
There is no Meta endpoint called “bulk delete Facebook Page posts.” If you have ever searched for one, you already know the trap: Business Suite can delete a small batch, Activity Log is click-hell, and Chrome extensions pretend there is a bulk API by driving the website UI. Under the hood, official deletion is still one HTTP call per post. DELETE https://graph.facebook.com/v21.0/{page-id}_{post-id} Authorization: Bearer {page-access-token}
A successful response is just: { "success": true }
Ten thousand posts means ten thousand of those calls. That is the whole architecture. With a Page access token and pages_manage_posts, Graph will delete regular Page posts the Page published: status updates photos that appear as feed items Reels that appear in the feed link shares Scan the feed (GET /…
